Teach libxml2 2.15.x's config.sub the iOS *simulator* triplet.

This is the modern-upstream half of a pair. meta.yaml routes any version that
does not start with "2.9." to this file (currently 2.15.3) and everything else
to mobile-2.9.x.patch. build.sh configures with `--host=$HOST_TRIPLET`, and
configure feeds that value to config.sub before it does anything else.

The config.sub shipped in 2.15.x already understands `*-apple-ios`, so the
device slice (aarch64-apple-ios) canonicalises fine. The simulator slices
arrive as `aarch64-apple-ios-simulator` / `x86_64-apple-ios-simulator`;
config.sub splits that tail into a kernel/os pair, does not recognise
`ios-simulator`, and configure dies with an `Invalid configuration ... not
recognized` error before a single file is compiled.

The patch adds one case to the `case $basic_os in` block: for
`ios-simulator*`, leave the kernel empty and keep the os string as given, so
the triplet validates. Nothing downstream depends on the canonical form -- the
triple only has to parse and to differ from the build machine's, which is what
makes configure treat this as a cross build. Actual device-vs-simulator
targeting comes from the compiler's -isysroot, which forge sets.

recipes/flet-libxslt/patches/mobile-1.1.45.patch is byte-identical, for the
same reason.

How this differs from its sibling mobile-2.9.x.patch: that one has to reach
into a much older config.sub, which knows neither `*-apple-ios` nor the
simulator suffix, and it additionally edits libxml2.syms. Neither is needed
here -- 2.15.x's config.sub is current, and upstream removed the libxml2.syms
version script around 2.10. The split into two version-suffixed patches was
made in PR #48 ("Bump libxml2/libxslt/lxml"), which notes that the new 2.15.x
patch "only carr[ies] an `ios-simulator*` case for modern `config.sub`; the old
`docb*` / `xmlDllMain` symbol tweaks are unnecessary against current upstream".

diff --git a/config.sub b/config.sub
--- a/config.sub
+++ b/config.sub
@@ -1323,6 +1323,10 @@
 	nto-qnx*)
 		kernel=nto
 		os=`echo "$basic_os" | sed -e 's|nto-qnx|qnx|'`
+		;;
+	ios-simulator*)
+		kernel=
+		os=$basic_os
 		;;
 	*-*)
 		# shellcheck disable=SC2162
